@meta task="auth-rewrite" lead="claude-1" agents="claude-1,claude-2,claude-3" target="2026-05-20"

@h1 Auth middleware rewrite [#root]
@p Replace the legacy session-token middleware with JWT plus refresh-token
@p rotation. Driven by compliance — legal flagged that session tokens were
@p stored in a way that does not satisfy SOC-2 requirements.

@h2 Subtasks [#tasks]
@ol [#task-list]
- extract token validation into a separate package
- design refresh-token rotation strategy
- migrate session store from Redis to encrypted Postgres column
- update integration tests
- write migration playbook

@h2 Status updates [#status]

@quote source="claude-1" [#status-t1]
> t1 complete: package `auth-tokens` extracted, see PR 482.
> tests green, no behavioural change.

@quote source="claude-2" [#status-t2]
> t2 in progress. Considering RFC 6749 sliding-window vs absolute-expiry.
> Need decision before t3 can start. Pinging lead.

@quote source="claude-3" [#status-t3]
> blocked on t2. Have drafted Postgres schema, see code below.

@code lang=sql [#schema-draft]
~~~
CREATE TABLE auth_tokens (
    id          UUID PRIMARY KEY,
    user_id     UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),
    token_hash  BYTEA NOT NULL,
    issued_at   TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    expires_at  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    revoked_at  TIMESTAMPTZ,
    UNIQUE (user_id, token_hash)
);
CREATE INDEX ON auth_tokens (expires_at) WHERE revoked_at IS NULL;
~~~

@h2 Decisions log [#decisions]
@ul
- 2026-05-09 — chose JWT (HS256) over PASETO; library maturity wins
- 2026-05-12 — refresh tokens rotate on every use, blast radius < 5 min
- 2026-05-15 — migration runs via dual-write window of 48h

